From b64b625df6322f5ca0e20fdcaa11ad00943b2117 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude sandbox <sandbox@local>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 09:11:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat: correction/review system, auto-approve timeout, VC
 rename fix, admin command cleanup
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Correction/review system (match_issues table, intake+outbound channels):
- match_issues table: serves both /correction-result and OCR-failure routing
- IssueResolveView/IssueResolveButton via discord.py 2.4 DynamicItem — survives
  bot restarts (unlike a plain View, which would silently stop working for
  buttons on messages posted before the current process started)
- /correction-result — host-only, Case A (blocks approve) and Case B
  (already-approved 'approved by mistake' short form)
- Friendly player-facing message + full technical detail routed separately
  to admins, at all 4 review-trigger points in match_submit

Auto-approve timeout (5 min default, was 3600s):
- matches.approval_deadline column, periodic sweep (discord.ext.tasks,
  same pattern as queue.py's cleanup_sweep) — DB-backed, restart-safe,
  one query covers any number of concurrent overdue matches
- has_open_issue guard is the SINGLE check both the manual Approve button
  and the sweep call through _do_approve — no separate timer-pause logic
  needed, filing a correction blocks both paths identically
- Shared _run_post_approval_cleanup/_do_approve helpers extracted so
  manual and auto-approve both get identical cleanup behavior

Admin commands (RO3-aware replacements for dead pre-RO3 commands):
- Removed admin-approve-match, admin-correct-stat — confirmed via code
  read they predate the RO3 rewrite, would silently corrupt state if used
  (never touch match_round_results or approve_ro3_match)
- Added admin-correct-round — round-scoped, validated against the same
  position/MVP-uniqueness rules _prepare_rounds already enforces. Real
  bug caught and fixed during build: win/loss must be derived from the
  round's actual final_score, NOT guessed from an existing delta's sign
  (a losing 1st-place MVP scores +2, a positive delta despite losing —
  that heuristic would have been backwards)
- Added admin-force-approve — calls the same _do_approve path as
  everything else, not a separate implementation
- default_permissions(manage_guild=True) on the Admin cog — hides admin
  commands from the picker for non-admins (UI hint; @admin_only() still
  does actual enforcement, kept as-is)

Smaller fixes:
- VC rename bug: was replacing the whole channel name on room-code share,
  dropping match_id entirely (CQ-1234 -> Defender · 123456). Now appends.
- /update-ign removed (IGN changes go through admin contact now)
- 'already submitted' vs other status-mismatch messages distinguished
- verification card notes MMR values are proposed, not yet applied
- fixed a stale matches.map reference in admin-review-queue (dead column
  removed earlier this session)
- schema.sql synced with what's actually live on Supabase (pending_verification,
  abandoned were added via ad-hoc migration earlier, never reflected here)

REQUIRED before live: run database/migration_005_correction_and_timeout.sql,
set ISSUE_INTAKE_CHANNEL_ID / ISSUE_RESOLVED_CHANNEL_ID in .env.
